<title>USA: Bell Atlantic, NYNEX see $200 mln more savings - NYT.</title>
<headline>Bell Atlantic, NYNEX see $200 mln more savings - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bell Atlantic and NYNEX Corp, who plan to merge, are pushing to generate $800 million in cost savings over three years instead of the $600 million first forecast, the New York Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Times cited an unnamed senior Bell Atlantic executive, who was quoted as saying that as part of the cost-saving effort, the companies might end up cutting more jobs than the 3,000 jobs they initially predicted.</p>
<p>But the Times quoted the executive as saying the companies had not set a target of 10,000 jobs in three to five years.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
